# File: tests/features/add_greeting_adler32_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/248-add-greeting-adler32-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the Adler-32 checksum of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Return the Adler-32 checksum of the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_adler32 is called with Ada and Ada Lovelace
    Then the results are the Python int values 312279879 and 1063257746

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Checksum the UTF-8 encoding of non-ASCII greetings
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_adler32 is called with Zo plus U+00EB
    Then the result is 400032888, the zlib Adler-32 of the UTF-8 encoded greeting

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_adler32 is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_adler32 of Ada
    Then it prints 312279879 and greeting_adler32 is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the unsigned UTF-8 Adler-32 result, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
